WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:33.030
<b>The Rich Girl and 

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.500
I'm exhausted, again.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.530
And the company commander 
wasn't even going hard on us.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.620
That was his regular exercise.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:45.520
<b>Nikolaus (24)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:45.520
<b>Hans (23)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.540
Huh? Hey, Hans. Look over there.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:49.310
A carriage in front of Nobu?

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:50.690
A nobleman.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:52.560
What are they doing in this 
run-down part of town?

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:53.890
You don't see that often.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:55.800
Oh, they're going into Nobu.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.480
I guess even the nobility 
knows about them now.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:00:59.900
Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.030
That place is full of surprises.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.880
Welcome!

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:04.860
Welcome.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:06.350
Here you go.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:07.440
A hot towel.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:12.380
<b>Johann Gustav (30)
Count of Badenburg</b>

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:12.380
<b>Hildegard (12)
Daughter of a viscount</b>

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.150
A hot... towel?

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:09.750
Yes.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:12.860
You can go ahead and use this to 
wipe your hands before your meal.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:15.040
I imagine it's something like a handkerchief.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.330
Thank you.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>Oh, it's warm.</i>

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:24.230
<i>This is very welcome on 
a cold day like this.</i>

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:26.950
<i>The service is as good as the rumors say.</i>

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.430
<i>A foreign land's letters, I suppose.</i>

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:34.200
<i>Such variety of menu options suggests 
the chef has highly refined skills.</i>

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.960
<i>This place has a nice atmosphere.</i>

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.490
<i>And yet...</i>

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:41.540
What may I bring you?

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:44.210
Something not stinky.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:45.460
Something not spicy.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:46.850
Something not sour.

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:47.920
Something not bitter.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.220
Something not hard.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:52.990
Something not bread, not tubers, not 
porridge, not eggs and not stew,

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:55.340
but something tasty.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:02:02.000
<i>My apologies, foreign person, for burdening 
you with Hildegard's impossible order.</i>

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:05.080
What do you say?
Do you think you can do it?

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:07.790
Let's see...
Something not stinky.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.270
Something not spicy.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:10.670
Something not sour.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:11.730
Something not bitter.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.140
Something not hard.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:17.230
Something not bread, not tubers, not 
porridge, not eggs and not stew,

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:18.900
but something tasty, right?

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.190
All right then.

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:21.750
Just a moment please.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:23.400
<i>Unfazed?</i>

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.620
<i>Not the reaction I expected.</i>

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:30.530
<i>No goods come through Aitheria 
during the long winter.</i>

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:38.550
<i>Even amongst renowned restaurants, we have 
yet to find one that can satisfy her.</i>

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:40.720
<i>What about this place, though?</i>

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.790
<i>The chef here looks completely unfazed.</i>

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:47.180
<i>What in the world will they serve her?</i>

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:49.060
Uncle Johann.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:49.770
Yes?

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.980
As you know, this is the last place.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:58.050
If this restaurant also fails to satisfy 
me, I will never speak to you again.

00:02:58.050 --> 00:02:59.550
I understand.

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:02.260
But there's also a matter of taste.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.120
Maybe the foreign cuisine of this...

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.060
Uncle!

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:06.230
Yes?

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:10.970
Who was it who promised to 
get me a dish I'd enjoy?

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:12.800
Well, that was...

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.920
I despise adults who lie.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:20.710
<i>I guess I raised her to 
be a bit too headstrong.</i>

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:24.210
<i>I took her in after my older 
brother and his wife died.</i>

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:29.750
<i>I did raise her to be a person worthy 
to inherit the viscount title,</i>

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:33.190
<i>but it is also true that 
I have spoiled her a little.</i>

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:38.410
<i>Since her wedding has been decided on, 
her stubbornness has only worsened.</i>

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.320
<i>Perhaps she is simply insecure.</i>

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:45.040
<i>After all, she hasn't even met 
the person who's to marry her.</i>

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:48.120
Pardon my reach, please.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:49.780
And what is this?

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.070
I'm going to light it now.

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:54.140
Please be careful.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:58.700
I see.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.950
It's a small, portable cooking pot.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:02.880
How convenient.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:06.920
Hildegard, isn't this the first 
time you've seen water boil?

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:08.540
Yes, this is the first time.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:10.860
<i>So they cook the food right 
in front of the guests and</i>

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:13.280
<i>have them eat it as soon as it is done.</i>

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:15.280
<i>This is superb.</i>

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:20.060
<i>Usually, the food gets cold while they 
have the retainers test for poison.</i>

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:24.800
<i>It's been years since 
I've eaten my food warm.</i>

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:28.600
<i>I'm looking forward to this.</i>

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:31.240
<i>Or, I'd like to, but so far, 
all I see floating in there is</i>

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:36.200
<i>something that looks like 
some sort of green skin?</i>

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:39.480
<i>Is this really something that 
isn't stinky, isn't spicy,</i>

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:44.760
<i>isn't sour, isn't bitter, isn't 
hard, but is actually delicious?</i>

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:47.160
I'm going to put the tofu in now.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:51.410
<i>What is this white, rectangle-shaped lump?</i>

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:54.410
<b>Wibble      wibble</b>

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:54.400
<i>I can't even begin to imagine 
what it tastes like.</i>

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.810
I'm putting in the vegetables, too.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:01.860
<i>Leafy vegetables and 
mushrooms, in the winter?</i>

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.670
<i>Where did they get them from?</i>

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:06.870
<i>No, that doesn't matter.</i>

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:10.180
<i>This scent is reminding 
me of how hungry I am.</i>

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.860
<i>Quickly. I want to eat quickly.</i>

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.530
Are you looking forward to 
the meal as well, Hildegard?

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.200
Whatever.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:25.600
Taishou, it's almost time.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:28.700
All right. I'm ready as well.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:43.250
<b>Thick~</b>

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:50.410
Please try it.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:55.000
<b>Nobu's special ankake yudofu 
(boiled tofu in a thick sauce)</b>

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:55.000
<b>Boiled tofu that warms your 
entire body is good, isn't it?</b>

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.040
This is our ankake yudofu.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.990
Please eat carefully, as it is very hot.

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:57.270
Ankake yudofu?

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:05.010
<b>Feathery</b>

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.550
I'll try it, too.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:23.930
<i>It's so warm!</i>

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:28.420
<i>And I love this creamy, softly crumbling 
texture. It's so wonderful.</i>

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.300
<b>Crumble</b>

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:34.980
<i>You don't even have to think about chewing 
it or what you do with your tongue.</i>

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:38.710
<i>Just this wonderful soft 
texture and warmth,</i>

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:41.940
<i>going down your throat and bestowing 
its warmth on your body.</i>

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:45.780
<i>This deliciousness goes perfectly
with the chill of winter.</i>

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:50.820
<i>The taste is simple, but that's 
a relief for the chilled body.</i>

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:54.450
<i>It warms the body from the inside.</i>

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:01.730
That's good!

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:09.190
It's not stinky, or spicy, 
or sour, or bitter, or hard.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:13.370
It's not bread, or tubers, or 
porridge, or eggs, or stew.

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:15.380
It's delicious!

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:18.730
I'm so glad you're satisfied.

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:21.120
I said too much.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.450
It's all right.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:25.740
This isn't enough for me 
to say I'm satisfied.

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:37.230
<i>She's just like my sister-in-law.</i>

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:44.010
<i>I keep thinking of her as a 
child, but she's grown a lot.</i>

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:46.300
Yes, that was okay.

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:51.550
How peculiar a sight, to see 
you not leave a single bite.

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:53.180
Uncle,

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:57.890
there's one problem though.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:07:59.390
And what is that?

00:07:59.390 --> 00:08:04.880
That... it wasn't... quite enough.

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:12.030
You must really have enjoyed it 
if you're asking for seconds.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:14.330
I told you, it's okay.

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:18.640
So could we please ask for another portion?

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:22.270
I'm very sorry, but there's 
no more ankake yudofu.

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:25.980
This was just the first course.

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:28.450
We'll be servings many 
other things after this.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:31.940
I'm done with the oden prep.

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:35.790
<b>Nobu's Specialty Oden</b>

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:35.790
<b>Not stinky, not spicy, and so on.
Warms you up!</b>

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:44.470
<b>Steam steam</b>

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:51.610
<b>Sizzle sizzle</b>

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:15.320
I never knew that such deliciousness 
existed in the world.

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:16.990
I'm so glad.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:19.930
Looks like I kept my promise after all.

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:22.510
You're right. It's too bad though.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:27.630
Looks like I'll have nothing to be 
a bother to you over after this.

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.430
Hildegard...

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:31.450
Uncle,

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:35.910
you don't have to worry about me anymore.

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:41.220
From now on, please take 
good care of yourself.

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.810
<i>I cannot believe this.</i>

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:51.230
<i>All along, I was the one who was not ready.</i>

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.390
Thank you very much.

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:11.310
<i>In two months, Hildegard 
is going to get married.</i>

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:15.510
<i>The least I can do until 
then is to bring her</i>

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:18.260
<i>to this restaurant once a week.</i>

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:31.270
Next up, is Nobu Plus!

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.040
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:37.560
Lightly flavored yudofu is 
good too, but when you want

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:42.500
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:40.360
something a bit more substantial, 
this recipe is for you.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.280
It's amazing!

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:48.560
Ryuuta Kijima is going to put his own 
spin on the dishes featured in Nobu!

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:49.510
<b>Ryuuta Kijima Creates Nobu Dishes</b>

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:51.030
This episode was great again, huh?

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:52.600
Hildegard-chan was so cute.

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:55.800
Actually, that Hildegard-san? 
I want to cook something for her!

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:56.150
<b>Hildegard</b>

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:59.310
Right. But could you make 
something for me first?

00:10:56.350 --> 00:11:03.250
<b>Ryuuta Kijima</b>

00:10:56.820 --> 00:11:03.250
<b>Grew up in a household where both his grandmother and his mother were culinary researchers,
so he got into cooking at an early age. Now he's a culinary researcher who's popular
for his simple but serious recipes and his fun presentation.</b>

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:00.380
Your answer?

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:01.180
No.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:01.580
What?

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:03.250
I said I want to make something 
for Hildegard-san.

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:07.800
Today, I was thinking of making something 
a bit more suited for drinking,

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:13.950
<b>Suited for drinking
A yudofu with more substance</b>

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.750
so a yudofu that has a bit more substance.

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:11.590
More suited for drinking, ergo me?

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:13.590
I am only thinking about Hildegard-san.

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:15.200
Why?! Sheesh!

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:18.960
<b>Soy milk yudofu with tan-tan sesame sauce
 [Ingredients (serves 2)]
 Firm tofu   1 block
 Green onion   1/2 stalk
 Mizuna   1/2 bunch
 Dashi kelp   10 cm
 Unprocessed soy milk   300 ml
 Water   300 ml
 
 (Tan-tan sesame sauce)
 White ground sesame   1.5 tablespoons
 Miso   1.5 tablespoons
 Sugar   1/2 tablespoon
 Layu (spicy sesame oil)   to taste
 Sanshou   to taste
 Yudofu broth   2-3 tablespoons</b>

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:18.940
The ingredients call for soy milk and ground 
sesame, so it'll have a rich taste!

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:22.380
This was used in the episode 
as well, this dashi kelp.

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:22.730
Right.

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:26.460
First, you put just the kelp and 
water into the pot to soften it.

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:28.900
That's key, softening it 
before you turn on the heat.

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:29.470
<b>Turn on the heat after the dashi kelp is soft</b>

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:29.860
I see.

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:33.780
This is half a pack of mizuna, but 
you can use however much you like.

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:38.970
It cooks really fast, so I think the best 
way is to keep adding more as you eat.

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:40.250
That way you can enjoy the texture, too.

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:44.650
The tofu, you can just cut 
it right into the pot.

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:48.140
I think cutting it into 4 or 6 
pieces is the right bite size.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.220
I like that move!

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:52.100
We'll boil it with this soy milk.

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:55.300
So while it is yudofu, since the 
soy milk has an actual flavor,

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:58.240
there's quite a bit of umami, 
and it has a bit of a punch.

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:00.630
And this soy milk, we're 
adding it at this point.

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:01.450
All right.

00:12:02.310 --> 00:12:03.700
The sauce we're making today...

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:04.080
Yes.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:05.400
Is tan-tan sesame sauce.

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:21.550
<b>Making of the tan-tan sesame sauce - Mix together - White ground sesame   1.5 tablespoons
Miso   1.5 tablespoons - Sugar   1/2 tablespoon - Salt  1/4 teaspoon
Yudofu broth   2-3 tablespoons - Layu (spicy sesame oil) to taste - Sanshou to taste</b>

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:10.190
The interplay of the sesame and 
the miso is divine! So good!

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:12.540
This might be a good sauce 
for shabu shabu as well.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:17.460
With my adult palate, I like a 
lot of layu and and sanshou.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:20.680
Please remember, a lot of both! Thanks!

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:23.900
I just remembered this while mixing this.

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:26.440
Hildegard-san doesn't like spicy either.

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:27.500
Ryuu-chan, that's right.

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:28.230
Ah man, I messed up.

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:29.550
Don't worry, I like it hot.

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:32.420
Anyway, the amount of layu and 
sanshou is really up to you.

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:35.400
The proteins solidifying on the 
surface here, this is called yuba.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:35.770
Uh-huh.

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:40.390
Before eating this yudofu, you can have 
this yuba with the sauce we just made,

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:44.910
<b>The yuba that forms when you heat soy milk 
is part of the joy this dish provides</b>

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:41.000
Right. That sounds great!

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:44.910
Or you could eat just the yuba with a wasabi 
soy sauce dip. That'll help you drink.

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:43.990
Wonderful!

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:50.040
The tofu is getting warm, so now once 
we briefly cook the mizuna, it's done.

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:51.310
Oh my, so quick.

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:56.170
Mizuna cooks really quickly, so you 
should eat it as soon as it's done.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:59.130
<b>Mizuna cooks really quickly, 
so cook it as you eat it</b>

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:59.150
You know, yudofu and other hot pot dishes, 
the fun of them is to eat while cooking,

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:02.860
to eat and drink and cook, 
and so forth and so on.

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:03.350
I know!

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:06.490
Normal yudofu made in broth is obviously 
really tasty too, but just by

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:13.170
<b>Soy milk yudofu with tan-tan sesame sauce</b>

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:10.540
adding this soy milk, the tofu 
gets really soft and fluffy.

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:12.130
Additionally, it helps 
you warm up even more.

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:15.330
It has a nice body to it too, so 
please do try making this at home.

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:15.920
Definitely.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:20.580
And now, as I cook the mizuna, 
let's have some tofu.

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:21.990
Ah, hot, hot.

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:26.110
This really has some substance.

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:29.910
It's a really easy but tasty interpretation. 
Everyone, please try this.

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:32.250
It'll be perfect as a snack to 
go with a nightcap as well!

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:58.010
